<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<?xml-model href="https://www.tei-c.org/release/xml/tei/custom/schema/relaxng/tei_odds.rng" type="application/xml" schematypens="http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0"?>
<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:eg="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>TEI Simler: A focused TEI customization for the Simler Digital Scholarly Edition</title>
        <author>Simler Project Team</author>
      </titleStmt>
      <publicationStmt>
        <p>Distributed with the Simler data repository; the schema and the rendering of the edition are
          both derived from this file.</p>
      </publicationStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <p>This ODD was created from scratch as a slim, project-focused replacement for the
          adapted <ref target="https://www.deutschestextarchiv.de/doku/basisformat/">DTA-Basisformat
          (DTABf)</ref> customization (<ident>basisformat_all_customized.odd</ident>), and carries all of
          the project's modifications of that customization. Its scope is derived from the encoding of
          Simler's <hi rend="italic">Teutsche Gedichte</hi>; it selects the elements, attributes and
          values the edition uses, and follows the documentation conventions of the TEI
          <ref target="https://github.com/TEIC/TEI/blob/dev/P5/Exemplars/tei_simplePrint.odd"
            >Simple Print (tei_simplePrint)</ref> exemplar — in particular, the appearance of the
          source is recorded with <gi>rendition</gi> declarations in <gi>tagsDecl</gi> referenced
          from the global <att>rendition</att> attribute.</p>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
    <encodingDesc>
      <projectDesc>
        <p>TEI Simler is a TEI P5 customization for the digital scholarly edition of the collected
          poems of the Zurich poet Johann Wilhelm Simler (1605–1672). Several editions of the
          <hi rend="italic">Teutsche Gedichte</hi> are transcribed (A 1648, B 1653, C 1663, D 1688
          and minor pieces); this schema serves the whole corpus. The transcription is a line- and
          page-faithful diplomatic rendering of early-modern printed books set mainly in Fraktur.</p>
      </projectDesc>
      <editorialDecl>
        <p>The transcription preserves the physical layout of the printed source: every printed line
          <emph>end</emph> is marked with <gi>lb</gi> (following the DTABf convention — the line break
          is set after the outermost closing element), every page with <gi>pb</gi>, and hyphenation
          across a line is encoded with <gi>lb</gi> <att>break</att>=<val>no</val> (the hyphen being
          retained). Verse is encoded with <gi>lg</gi> and <gi>l</gi>; front matter with
          <gi>front</gi>, <gi>titlePage</gi> and typed <gi>div</gi>. The appearance of the source is
          recorded on <att>rendition</att> using the pointer tokens declared in <gi>tagsDecl</gi>.</p>
        <p>Obvious printing errors are corrected with <gi>choice</gi> (<gi>sic</gi>/<gi>corr</gi>);
          unreadable passages with <gi>unclear</gi>; editorially supplied text with <gi>supplied</gi>.
          Named entities are tagged with <gi>rs</gi> carrying <att>type</att> and a typed
          <att>key</att>. Editorial comments are anchored with <gi>anchor</gi> pairs and held in
          <gi>note</gi>.</p>
        <p>The source files are a work in progress; content models and value lists are kept
          deliberately permissive (suggested rather than closed value lists) so that minor encoding
          variation does not invalidate a document.</p>
      </editorialDecl>
      <tagsDecl>
        <!-- Source appearance, declared once and pointed to from @rendition. The CSS records how
             the passage looks in the SOURCE; custom properties are the edition's design tokens. -->
        <rendition xml:id="aq" scheme="css">font-family: var(--f-antiqua);</rendition><!-- Antiqua within Fraktur -->
        <rendition xml:id="fr" scheme="css">font-family: var(--f-text);</rendition><!-- Fraktur within Antiqua -->
        <rendition xml:id="b" scheme="css">font-weight: 600;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="i" scheme="css">font-style: italic;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="c" scheme="css">text-align: center;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="right" scheme="css">text-align: right;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="g" scheme="css">letter-spacing: 0.125em;</rendition><!-- gesperrt -->
        <rendition xml:id="k" scheme="css">font-variant: small-caps;</rendition><!-- Kapitälchen -->
        <rendition xml:id="in" scheme="css">float: left; font-size: 2.1em; line-height: 0.86; padding-right: 0.06em; font-weight: 500;</rendition><!-- Initiale -->
        <rendition xml:id="sup" scheme="css">vertical-align: super; font-size: smaller;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="larger" scheme="css">font-size: larger;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="smaller" scheme="css">font-size: smaller;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="et" scheme="css">text-indent: 2em;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="et2" scheme="css">text-indent: 4em;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="et3" scheme="css">text-indent: 6em;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="hr" scheme="css">display: block; border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--c-line)); width: 30%; margin: 1.2em auto;</rendition>
        <!-- The Buchstabwechsel pages: an interleaved two-column setting (read row by row, so the
             lines alternate left and right) whose acrostic lines carry marginal letters, set in the
             line's padding. The line boxes are laid out by the l models. -->
        <rendition xml:id="twocol" scheme="css">--acro-body: 1.45em; --acro-fin: 1.25em; --indent-step: 0.5em; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; column-gap: 1.3em; align-items: baseline;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="acrostic" scheme="css">position: relative;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="acroInit" scheme="css">position: absolute; left: 0; font-weight: 600;</rendition>
        <rendition xml:id="acroFin" scheme="css">position: absolute; right: 0; font-weight: 600;</rendition>
      </tagsDecl>
    </encodingDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text>
    <body>
      <head>TEI Simler: A focused TEI customization for the Simler Digital Scholarly Edition</head>

      <p>This document defines TEI Simler, a slim customization of the
        <ref target="https://tei-c.org/guidelines/">TEI Guidelines</ref> for the digital scholarly
        edition of Johann Wilhelm Simler's <hi rend="italic">Teutsche Gedichte</hi>. It keeps the
        project's modifications of the DTABf-derived schema while excluding the DTABf modules,
        elements and attributes that the project does not use.</p>

      <p>Each source document is a printed edition encoded within a <gi>TEI</gi> element holding a
        <gi>teiHeader</gi> and one <gi>text</gi>. The <gi>text</gi> may open with <gi>front</gi>
        matter (title page, dedication, frontispiece) and continues with a <gi>body</gi> containing a
        hierarchy of <gi>div</gi> elements (book → poem) whose verse is encoded with <gi>lg</gi> and
        <gi>l</gi>.</p>

      <p>The Processing Model renders the edition. Each element takes the first <gi>model</gi> whose
        <att>predicate</att> holds; a <gi>modelSequence</gi> renders each of its models whose
        predicate holds, one after the other. A <gi>modelGrp</gi>'s <gi>outputRendition</gi> styles
        all of its models; a styled model among several names its class with <att>cssClass</att>.
        Predicates see the text as encoded. Params are
        XPath: the nodes they select are rendered by their own models, anything else as text;
        params named <val>--…</val> become CSS custom properties of the rendered element,
        <val>data-…</val> its attributes. Models with an <att>output</att> belong to that output
        and take precedence over the base models there. <val>page</val>, on <gi>TEI</gi>, names
        what the page shows around the text. <val>plain</val>, the text of the search index, is
        rendered on its own. <val>normalized</val> (the reading text) and <val>entities</val> (entity
        highlighting) are views over the base rendering that can be switched on and off: a view's
        model omits the element, restyles it, or gives the same behaviour other params — an
        <val>alternate</val> shows the view's own default; a view's <gi>modelSequence</gi> does so
        model by model for the base sequence. The source appearance
        (<att>rendition</att>) is carried where the model sets <att>useSourceRendition</att>; a model
        that lays out the rendition itself does without. Colours, fonts and measures are the
        edition's design tokens (CSS custom properties).</p>

      <schemaSpec ident="tei_simler" start="TEI" prefix="tei_" targetLang="de" docLang="en">

        <!-- ===================================================================
             MODULES — only those the Simler edition uses
             =================================================================== -->
        <moduleRef key="header" include="teiHeader fileDesc titleStmt editionStmt edition publicationStmt sourceDesc biblFull extent idno encodingDesc editorialDecl profileDesc langUsage language textClass classCode"/>
        <moduleRef key="core" include="p lb pb head label hi l lg list item rs choice sic corr unclear milestone note num title author bibl name date pubPlace publisher ref cit quote abbr cb measure respStmt resp"/>
        <moduleRef key="textstructure" include="TEI text front body div titlePage titlePart docTitle docAuthor docImprint docDate docEdition closer signed salute dateline epigraph byline"/>
        <moduleRef key="namesdates" include="persName surname forename"/>
        <moduleRef key="msdescription" include="msDesc msIdentifier repository physDesc typeDesc"/>
        <moduleRef key="transcr" include="fw supplied space"/>
        <moduleRef key="figures" include="figure"/>
        <moduleRef key="linking" include="anchor"/>
        <moduleRef key="tei"/>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             ATTRIBUTE CLASSES — light trimming; keep behaviour permissive
             =================================================================== -->
        <classSpec type="atts" ident="att.cmc" mode="delete"/>
        <classSpec type="atts" ident="att.global.change" mode="delete"/>
        <classSpec type="atts" ident="att.global" mode="change">
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="xml:base" mode="delete"/>
            <attDef ident="xml:space" mode="delete"/>
          </attList>
        </classSpec>

        <!-- @rendition: pointer tokens declared in tagsDecl. As in tei_simplePrint the value space is
             not closed: new appearance tokens are added by declaring them in tagsDecl. -->
        <classSpec type="atts" ident="att.global.rendition" mode="change">
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="rend" mode="delete"/>
            <attDef ident="style" mode="delete"/>
            <attDef ident="rendition" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <desc>One or more pointers to <gi>rendition</gi> elements in <gi>tagsDecl</gi>,
                recording the appearance of the source passage (e.g. <val>#aq</val>,
                <val>#et #aq</val>).</desc>
              <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                <dataRef key="teidata.pointer"/>
              </datatype>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
        </classSpec>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             REUSABLE CONTENT — phrase-level model shared across the transcription
             =================================================================== -->
        <macroSpec ident="macro.simlerInline" mode="add">
          <desc>The phrase-level content shared by the transcription elements: text interspersed with
            highlighting, entity references, editorial interventions, note anchors and line/page/column
            breaks.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/>
              <elementRef key="hi"/>
              <elementRef key="rs"/>
              <elementRef key="choice"/>
              <elementRef key="sic"/>
              <elementRef key="corr"/>
              <elementRef key="unclear"/>
              <elementRef key="supplied"/>
              <elementRef key="num"/>
              <elementRef key="note"/>
              <elementRef key="anchor"/>
              <elementRef key="abbr"/>
              <elementRef key="fw"/>
              <elementRef key="head"/>
              <elementRef key="lb"/>
              <elementRef key="pb"/>
              <elementRef key="cb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
        </macroSpec>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             ROOT, HEADER
             =================================================================== -->
        <elementSpec ident="TEI" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <desc>The root element of a Simler edition document: one <gi>teiHeader</gi> followed by one
            <gi>text</gi>. <att>type</att> is required.</desc>
          <content>
            <sequence>
              <elementRef key="teiHeader"/>
              <elementRef key="text"/>
            </sequence>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="req">
              <valList type="closed" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="simler-framework"><desc>Simler edition document</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <model behaviour="text"/>
          <!-- what the page shows around the text: its title, the facsimile, the entities it names -->
          <model output="page" behaviour="metadata">
            <param name="title" value="normalize-space(teiHeader/fileDesc/titleStmt/title[1])"/>
            <param name="manifest" value="normalize-space((descendant::idno[@type='URLIIIF'])[1])"/>
            <param name="pages" value="descendant::pb/@facs"/>
            <param name="entities" value="descendant::rs/@key"/>
          </model>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <TEI type="simler-framework"><teiHeader><!-- ... --></teiHeader><text><!-- ... --></text></TEI>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="teiHeader" module="header" mode="change">
          <desc>Document metadata: a <gi>fileDesc</gi>, an optional <gi>encodingDesc</gi> and an
            optional (possibly empty) <gi>profileDesc</gi>.</desc>
          <content>
            <sequence>
              <elementRef key="fileDesc"/>
              <elementRef key="encodingDesc" minOccurs="0"/>
              <elementRef key="profileDesc" minOccurs="0"/>
            </sequence>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="metadata"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="fileDesc" module="header" mode="change">
          <desc>The bibliographic description of the file.</desc>
          <content>
            <sequence>
              <elementRef key="titleStmt"/>
              <elementRef key="editionStmt" minOccurs="0"/>
              <elementRef key="publicationStmt"/>
              <elementRef key="sourceDesc"/>
            </sequence>
          </content>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="titleStmt" module="header" mode="change">
          <desc>One or more <gi>title</gi>s, optional <gi>author</gi>s and statements of
            responsibility.</desc>
          <content>
            <sequence>
              <elementRef key="title" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
              <elementRef key="author" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
              <elementRef key="respStmt" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
            </sequence>
          </content>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="title" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A title of the edited text.</desc>
          <content><macroRef key="macro.phraseSeq"/></content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="main"><desc>main title</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="sub"><desc>subtitle</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
            <attDef ident="level" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="closed" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="a"><desc>analytic: an article or a part</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="j"><desc>a journal</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="m"><desc>a monograph: in the header, the printed volume</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="s"><desc>a series</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <title type="main">TEIL 3 VON: Johann-Wilhelm Simlers teutscher Getichten die dritte
                […] Aussfertigung</title>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="author" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>The author of the edited text, normally a structured <gi>persName</gi>.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="persName"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <author><persName ref="http://d-nb.info/gnd/119151693"><surname>Simler</surname><forename>Johann
                Wilhelm</forename></persName></author>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="persName" module="namesdates" mode="change">
          <desc>A personal name; <att>ref</att> links to an external authority record (GND).</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="surname"/><elementRef key="forename"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="editionStmt" module="header" mode="change">
          <content><elementRef key="edition"/></content>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="edition" module="header" mode="change">
          <content><macroRef key="macro.phraseSeq"/></content>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <edition>Vollständige digitalisierte Ausgabe.</edition>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="publicationStmt" module="header" mode="change">
          <desc>The publication statement: one or more paragraphs, or structured
            publisher/place/date.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="p"/>
              <elementRef key="publisher"/>
              <elementRef key="pubPlace"/>
              <elementRef key="date"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <publicationStmt><p>unknown</p></publicationStmt>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="sourceDesc" module="header" mode="change">
          <desc>Describes the digitised printed source: its bibliographic record (<gi>biblFull</gi> from
            the DTA import, or a loose <gi>bibl</gi>) and the physical copy (<gi>msDesc</gi>).</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="bibl"/><elementRef key="biblFull"/><elementRef key="msDesc"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="bibl" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A loosely structured bibliographic reference holding the identifiers of the
            digitised source.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="idno"/><elementRef key="title"/><elementRef key="author"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="M"><desc>monograph</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <bibl><idno type="URLIIIF">https://www.e-rara.ch/i3f/v20/4049159/manifest</idno></bibl>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="idno" module="header" mode="change">
          <desc>An identifier or URI for the source.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="idno"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="URLIIIF"><desc>URL of the IIIF presentation manifest; its root is also the
                  root of the page images named by <att>facs</att></desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="URLImages"><desc>URL of the page images</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="URLCatalogue"><desc>URL of the library catalogue record</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="DOI"><desc>DOI of the digitised copy</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="Transkribus"><desc>Transkribus document/collection identifier</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="shelfmark"><desc>library shelfmark of the printed copy</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="date" module="core" mode="change">
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="publication"><desc>date of publication of the source</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="firstPublication"><desc>date of first publication</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="importDTA"><desc>date of the DTA import</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="measure" module="core" mode="change">
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="pages"><desc>number of pages</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="publisher" module="core" mode="change">
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/><elementRef key="name"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="inline"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="profileDesc" module="header" mode="change">
          <desc>Optional descriptive profile (language usage, classification). May be empty.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="langUsage"/><elementRef key="textClass"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             TEXT STRUCTURE
             =================================================================== -->
        <elementSpec ident="text" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <desc>The transcribed text: an optional <gi>front</gi> and a <gi>body</gi>. A front-matter
            volume may carry <gi>front</gi> without a <gi>body</gi>.</desc>
          <content>
            <sequence>
              <elementRef key="front" minOccurs="0"/>
              <elementRef key="body" minOccurs="0"/>
            </sequence>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="block">
            <outputRendition>font-size: var(--fs-text); line-height: var(--lh-text); hyphens: none; max-width: var(--measure); font-variant-ligatures: common-ligatures;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="front" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <desc>Front matter: title page(s) and prefatory divisions (dedication, frontispiece).</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="titlePage"/><elementRef key="div"/><elementRef key="figure"/>
              <elementRef key="milestone"/><elementRef key="lb"/><elementRef key="pb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="text"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="body" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <desc>The body of the document, holding the page/line stream and the hierarchy of
            structural divisions. A document not yet transcribed holds a single empty <gi>p</gi>.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="div"/><elementRef key="lg"/><elementRef key="l"/><elementRef key="p"/>
              <elementRef key="head"/><elementRef key="pb"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
              <elementRef key="milestone"/><elementRef key="fw"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="text"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="div" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <desc>A structural division — a book, a group of poems, or an individual poem. <att>type</att>
            classifies the division; <att>n</att> records its level/running number.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/>
              <elementRef key="div"/><elementRef key="head"/><elementRef key="lg"/><elementRef key="l"/>
              <elementRef key="p"/><elementRef key="list"/><elementRef key="label"/>
              <elementRef key="closer"/><elementRef key="epigraph"/><elementRef key="figure"/>
              <elementRef key="note"/><elementRef key="fw"/><elementRef key="cb"/>
              <elementRef key="anchor"/><elementRef key="milestone"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
              <elementRef key="pb"/><elementRef key="hi"/><elementRef key="rs"/>
              <elementRef key="choice"/><elementRef key="unclear"/><elementRef key="supplied"/>
              <elementRef key="num"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="poem"><desc>an individual poem</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="poem-div"><desc>a group of poems</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="stanza-div"><desc>a stanza of a strophic poem</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="dedication"><desc>a dedication</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="frontispiece"><desc>a frontispiece</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="letter"><desc>a letter</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="preface"><desc>a preface</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="music"><desc>notated music (Noten)</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <!-- a division directly after another one is set apart from it -->
          <model cssClass="div-after-div" predicate="preceding-sibling::*[not(self::lb or self::pb or self::fw or self::cb or self::milestone or self::anchor)][1][self::div]" behaviour="section">
            <outputRendition>margin-top: 2rem;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model behaviour="section"/>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <div n="3" type="poem">
                <head rendition="#c"><hi rendition="#aq">III.</hi></head>
                <lb/>
                <lg type="poem"><!-- ... --></lg>
              </div>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===== title page ===== -->
        <elementSpec ident="titlePage" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <desc>A title page transcribed within <gi>front</gi>.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="docTitle"/><elementRef key="titlePart"/><elementRef key="docAuthor"/>
              <elementRef key="docImprint"/><elementRef key="docDate"/><elementRef key="docEdition"/>
              <elementRef key="figure"/><elementRef key="label"/><elementRef key="milestone"/>
              <elementRef key="lb"/><elementRef key="pb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="main"><desc>the main title page</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <model behaviour="section">
            <outputRendition>text-align: center;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="docTitle" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="titlePart"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="block">
            <outputRendition>margin: 1.2em 0;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="titlePart" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="hi"/><elementRef key="lb"/><elementRef key="list"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="main"/><valItem ident="desc"/>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <model behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>margin: 0.4em 0;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="docAuthor" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true"/>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="docImprint" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="hi"/><elementRef key="pubPlace"/>
              <elementRef key="publisher"/><elementRef key="docDate"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true"/>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="docEdition" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <model behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true"/>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="docDate" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="inline"/>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="pubPlace" module="core" mode="change">
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="inline"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             VERSE
             =================================================================== -->
        <elementSpec ident="lg" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A group of verse lines — in the Simler edition typically a poem
            (<att>type</att>=<val>poem</val>) or a sub-group/stanza.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="l"/><elementRef key="lg"/><elementRef key="head"/>
              <elementRef key="label"/><elementRef key="p"/><elementRef key="note"/>
              <elementRef key="fw"/><elementRef key="figure"/><elementRef key="anchor"/>
              <elementRef key="cb"/><elementRef key="milestone"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
              <elementRef key="pb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="poem"><desc>a poem</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="poem-subgroup"><desc>a sub-group of a poem</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="stanza"><desc>a stanza</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
            <attDef ident="n" mode="change" usage="opt"/>
          </attList>
          <model cssClass="lg-inner" predicate="ancestor::lg" behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>margin: 0.9em 0;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="lg-outer" behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>margin: 1.3em 0;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <lg type="poem">
                <l><hi rendition="#in">W</hi>Er schälk’ und spötter fleucht/ und Gottes wort be<lb break="no"/>trachtet/</l>
                <lb/>
                <l rendition="#et">der gru&#x364;net wie ein baum an einem wasserfluß/</l>
              </lg>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="l" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A single verse line. <att>rendition</att> records the indentation of the printed
            line; line/word breaks of the setting are encoded with <gi>lb</gi>.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="hi"/><elementRef key="rs"/><elementRef key="choice"/>
              <elementRef key="unclear"/><elementRef key="supplied"/><elementRef key="num"/>
              <elementRef key="abbr"/><elementRef key="label"/><elementRef key="note"/>
              <elementRef key="anchor"/><elementRef key="space"/><elementRef key="fw"/>
              <elementRef key="lb"/><elementRef key="pb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="n" mode="change" usage="opt"/>
            <attDef ident="next" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <desc>The next part of a verse line the print splits, e.g. by a heading or a page;
                <att>prev</att> points back. So also on <gi>div</gi> and <gi>head</gi>.</desc>
            </attDef>
            <attDef ident="prev" mode="change" usage="opt"/>
          </attList>
          <!-- A verse line hangs: an overlong line wraps indented, and @rendition indents are counted
               from the hanging edge. On a two-column page the grid cell is the line box. -->
          <modelGrp useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>margin: 0; line-height: var(--lh-text); padding-left: 1.6em; text-indent: -1.6em;</outputRendition>
            <!-- On a two-column page the lines alternate between the columns. An acrostic line starts
                 behind its marginal letter, and so does an indented line in a column that has them;
                 a closing letter keeps the line's end clear. The model lays out @rendition itself. -->
            <model predicate="parent::lg[contains-token(@rendition, '#twocol')]" behaviour="block" cssClass="l-twocol" useSourceRendition="false">
              <param name="--acro" value="if (contains-token(@rendition, '#acrostic') or (contains-token(@rendition, '#et') or contains-token(@rendition, '#et2')) and (preceding-sibling::l[position() mod 2 = 0], following-sibling::l[position() mod 2 = 0])[contains-token(@rendition, '#acrostic')]) then 1 else 0"/>
              <param name="--fin" value="if (descendant::*[contains-token(@rendition, '#acroFin')]) then 1 else 0"/>
              <param name="--indent" value="if (contains-token(@rendition, '#et2')) then 2 else if (contains-token(@rendition, '#et')) then 1 else 0"/>
              <outputRendition>min-width: 0; position: relative; text-indent: 0; padding-left: calc(var(--acro) * var(--acro-body) + var(--indent) * var(--indent-step)); padding-right: calc(var(--fin) * (var(--acro-fin) + 0.1em));</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model predicate="contains-token(@rendition, '#et')" behaviour="block" cssClass="l-et">
              <outputRendition>text-indent: 0.4em;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model predicate="contains-token(@rendition, '#et2')" behaviour="block" cssClass="l-et2">
              <outputRendition>text-indent: 2.4em;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model predicate="contains-token(@rendition, '#et3')" behaviour="block" cssClass="l-et3">
              <outputRendition>text-indent: 4.4em;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model behaviour="block"/>
          </modelGrp>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <l rendition="#et">der wird <rs type="place" key="place_027">Sion</rs>sfeind’ auch straffen sonder fehl.</l>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             PHRASE-LEVEL TRANSCRIPTION
             =================================================================== -->
        <elementSpec ident="hi" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A typographically distinct span of the source. <att>rendition</att> is required on
            <gi>hi</gi> (it is optional elsewhere) and points to one or more <gi>rendition</gi>
            declarations in <gi>tagsDecl</gi>; tokens combine (e.g. <val>#aq #b</val>). <gi>hi</gi>
            may nest. The renditions of a line or block — alignment (<val>#c</val>,
            <val>#right</val>) and indent (<val>#et</val>, <val>#et2</val>, <val>#et3</val>) — are
            recorded on the block, not on <gi>hi</gi>.</desc>
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <constraintSpec ident="hi-block-rendition" scheme="schematron">
            <desc>Alignment and indent are properties of a line or block: they are recorded on the
              block element, where they take effect.</desc>
            <constraint>
              <sch:rule xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron"
                context="tei:hi[tokenize(@rendition, '\s+') = ('#c', '#right', '#et', '#et2', '#et3')]">
                <sch:report role="warning" test="true()">[S-HI] Alignment and indent (#c, #right,
                  #et, #et2, #et3) belong on the enclosing block (head, p, l, …), not on hi.</sch:report>
              </sch:rule>
            </constraint>
          </constraintSpec>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="rendition" mode="change" usage="req"/>
          </attList>
          <!-- An initial drops only at the head of running prose: not in verse, not nested, not
               among several initials (an author line "J(ohann) W(ilhelm) S(imler)"), not centred. -->
          <model cssClass="hi-initial-inline" predicate="contains-token(@rendition, '#in') and (ancestor::l or ancestor::hi or ancestor::titlePage or ancestor::*[contains-token(@rendition, '#c')] or preceding-sibling::*[contains-token(@rendition, '#in')] or following-sibling::*[contains-token(@rendition, '#in')])" behaviour="inline" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>float: none; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: inherit;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <!-- Fallback for an indent left on a hi: on a line of its own within a block, the hi is
               that line, since a span cannot be indented. -->
          <model predicate="(contains-token(@rendition, '#et') or contains-token(@rendition, '#et2') or contains-token(@rendition, '#et3')) and (parent::head or parent::p or parent::l or parent::salute or parent::signed or parent::dateline or parent::closer or parent::titlePart or parent::docAuthor or parent::item) and (not(preceding-sibling::*) or preceding-sibling::*[1][self::lb]) and (not(following-sibling::*) or following-sibling::*[1][self::lb])" behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true"/>
          <model behaviour="inline" useSourceRendition="true"/>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <head rendition="#c"><hi rendition="#b">Aller<lb/> Psalmen Davids Haubt<lb break="no"/>begriff/</hi></head>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="head" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A heading of a <gi>div</gi>, <gi>lg</gi>, <gi>list</gi> or <gi>figure</gi>.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="hi"/><elementRef key="label"/><elementRef key="num"/>
              <elementRef key="rs"/><elementRef key="choice"/><elementRef key="unclear"/>
              <elementRef key="supplied"/><elementRef key="note"/><elementRef key="fw"/>
              <elementRef key="anchor"/><elementRef key="lb"/><elementRef key="pb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="n" mode="change" usage="opt"/>
          </attList>
          <!-- Only a division's head is a document heading, one level below its division; in an
               lg it is a stanza number, in a list or figure a caption. -->
          <modelGrp useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 600; text-wrap: balance;</outputRendition>
            <model cssClass="head-first" predicate="parent::div and not(preceding-sibling::*[not(self::lb or self::pb or self::fw or self::cb or self::milestone or self::anchor)])" behaviour="heading">
              <param name="level" value="count(ancestor::div) + 1"/>
              <outputRendition>margin: 0 0 0.7em;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model cssClass="head-div" predicate="parent::div" behaviour="heading">
              <param name="level" value="count(ancestor::div) + 1"/>
              <outputRendition>margin: 1.6em 0 0.7em;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model cssClass="head-stanza" predicate="parent::lg" behaviour="paragraph">
              <outputRendition>font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.72em; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: rgb(var(--c-muted)); margin: 0 0 0.25em;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model cssClass="head-caption" predicate="parent::list or parent::figure" behaviour="paragraph">
              <outputRendition>margin: 0 0 0.3em;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model cssClass="head-other" behaviour="paragraph">
              <outputRendition>margin: 1.6em 0 0.7em;</outputRendition>
            </model>
          </modelGrp>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <head rendition="#c">
                <label>[1.]</label>
                <lb/>
                <hi rendition="#b">[Das erst bu&#x364;ch der Psalmen.]</hi>
              </head>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="label" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A label, typically the (often editorially supplied, bracketed) number of a heading or
            poem.</desc>
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>font-weight: 500;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples"><label>[2.]</label></egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="num" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A number (Roman or Arabic) marked as such in the source.</desc>
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="inline"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="p" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A prose paragraph (e.g. closing formulae of a book, captions, header notes).</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="hi"/><elementRef key="rs"/><elementRef key="choice"/>
              <elementRef key="unclear"/><elementRef key="supplied"/><elementRef key="num"/>
              <elementRef key="note"/><elementRef key="ref"/><elementRef key="lg"/>
              <elementRef key="anchor"/><elementRef key="fw"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
              <elementRef key="pb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="paragraph" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>margin: 0.9em 0;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <p rendition="#c"><hi rendition="#smaller">Ende des ersten buchs der<lb/> Psalmen Davids.</hi></p>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===== entity reference ===== -->
        <elementSpec ident="rs" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A referencing string identifying a named entity. <att>type</att> classifies the
            entity; <att>key</att> is the typed identifier of the entry in the project registers
            (its prefix should match <att>type</att>).</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="hi"/><elementRef key="rs"/><elementRef key="choice"/>
              <elementRef key="unclear"/><elementRef key="supplied"/><elementRef key="note"/>
              <elementRef key="anchor"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <constraintSpec ident="rs-key" scheme="schematron">
            <desc>A key names an entry of the register its <att>type</att> belongs to; <val>org</val>
              is in the institutions, <val>bibl</val> in the works.</desc>
            <constraint>
              <sch:rule xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" context="tei:rs">
                <sch:let name="register" value="if (@type = 'org') then 'institution' else if (@type = 'bibl') then 'work' else string(@type)"/>
                <sch:assert test="matches(@key, concat('^', $register, '_\d+$'))">[S-RK] "<sch:value-of
                  select="@key"/>" is not a key of the <sch:value-of select="$register"/> register.</sch:assert>
              </sch:rule>
            </constraint>
          </constraintSpec>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="req">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="person"><desc>person</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="place"><desc>place</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="org"><desc>organisation</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="institution"><desc>institution</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="work"><desc>literary work</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="bibl"><desc>a Bible reference (never the research bibliography)</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
            <attDef ident="key" mode="change" usage="req">
              <desc>The entry in the register of <att>type</att>, as <val>{register}_{number}</val>
                (e.g. <val>person_049</val>); see <ident>rs-key</ident>.</desc>
              <datatype><dataRef key="teidata.text"/></datatype>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <model behaviour="inline"/>
          <!-- entity highlighting, colour-coded by type -->
          <model cssClass="entity-person" output="entities" predicate="@type='person'" behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-person)); text-decoration: underline solid; text-underline-offset: 0.22em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="entity-place" output="entities" predicate="@type='place'" behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-place)); text-decoration: underline solid; text-underline-offset: 0.22em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="entity-work" output="entities" predicate="@type='work'" behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-work)); text-decoration: underline dashed; text-underline-offset: 0.22em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="entity-org" output="entities" predicate="@type='org'" behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-org)); text-decoration: underline solid; text-underline-offset: 0.22em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="entity-institution" output="entities" predicate="@type='institution'" behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-institution)); text-decoration: underline dotted; text-underline-offset: 0.22em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="entity-bibl" output="entities" predicate="@type='bibl'" behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-bibl)); text-decoration: underline dotted; text-underline-offset: 0.22em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <l>Der <rs type="person" key="person_049">David</rs> setzt auf Gott sein hoffnung und vertrauen/</l>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===== editorial interventions: the print, or in the reading text the correction ===== -->
        <elementSpec ident="choice" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>Groups the source reading (<gi>sic</gi>) and its editorial correction
            (<gi>corr</gi>), in either order.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="sic"/><elementRef key="corr"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <!-- the print, and in the reading text the correction; the search finds both -->
          <model predicate="sic and corr" behaviour="alternate">
            <param name="default" value="sic"/>
            <param name="alternate" value="corr"/>
          </model>
          <model behaviour="inline"/>
          <model output="normalized" predicate="sic and corr" behaviour="alternate">
            <param name="default" value="corr"/>
            <param name="alternate" value="sic"/>
          </model>
          <model output="plain" predicate="sic and corr" behaviour="inline">
            <param name="content" value="(sic, ' ', corr)"/>
          </model>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <l>Wiewol ich krankner mir gedult hab <choice><sic>fu&#x364;rgenommen</sic><corr>fürgenommen</corr></choice>/</l>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="sic" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>The reading actually present in the source, retained unchanged.</desc>
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="inline"/>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="corr" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>The editorial correction of an obvious printing error.</desc>
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <!-- an editorial correction is marked as one: dotted, never silent -->
          <model behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>text-decoration: underline dotted rgb(var(--c-muted)); text-underline-offset: 0.22em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="supplied" module="transcr" mode="change">
          <desc>Text supplied by the editors where the source is missing or illegible.
            <att>cert</att> may record the confidence of the supplement.</desc>
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="cert" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="high"/><valItem ident="low"/>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <!-- The brackets are the edition's text, not the search's. -->
          <modelSequence>
            <model cssClass="supplied-bracket" behaviour="inline">
              <param name="content" value="'['"/>
              <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-muted));</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model behaviour="inline"/>
            <model cssClass="supplied-bracket" behaviour="inline">
              <param name="content" value="']'"/>
              <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-muted));</outputRendition>
            </model>
          </modelSequence>
          <modelSequence output="plain">
            <model behaviour="omit"/>
            <model behaviour="inline"/>
            <model behaviour="omit"/>
          </modelSequence>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="unclear" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A passage that cannot be read with certainty; <att>reason</att> records why.</desc>
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="reason" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="uncleanPrint"><desc>illegible because of poor / unclean printing</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="covered"><desc>covered or obscured on the page</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <model behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>text-decoration: underline wavy rgb(var(--c-muted) / 0.7); text-underline-offset: 0.22em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <l rendition="#et">die <unclear reason="uncleanPrint">kind</unclear> und […]</l>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="abbr" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>An abbreviation as it appears in the source.</desc>
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="inline"/>
          <model output="normalized" predicate="parent::choice" behaviour="omit"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             NOTES, LISTS, FIGURES, QUOTATIONS
             =================================================================== -->
        <elementSpec ident="note" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A note. Editorial notes (<val>annotation</val>) comment on a range delimited by an
            <gi>anchor</gi> and <att>targetEnd</att>, or without one on the whole division; Bible
            references, speaker names and marginalia are printed in the source.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="p"/><elementRef key="hi"/><elementRef key="rs"/>
              <elementRef key="choice"/><elementRef key="unclear"/><elementRef key="supplied"/>
              <elementRef key="note"/><elementRef key="anchor"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <constraintSpec ident="note-range" scheme="schematron">
            <desc>A range comment runs from the <gi>anchor</gi> its <att>targetEnd</att> names, which
              precedes it, to the note.</desc>
            <constraint>
              <sch:rule xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" context="tei:note[@targetEnd]">
                <sch:let name="id" value="replace(@targetEnd, '^#', '')"/>
                <sch:assert test="preceding::tei:anchor[@xml:id = $id]">[S-NR] targetEnd names no
                  preceding anchor.</sch:assert>
              </sch:rule>
            </constraint>
          </constraintSpec>
          <constraintSpec ident="note-type" scheme="schematron">
            <desc>A note says what it is: a range comment by <att>targetEnd</att>, any other by
              <att>type</att>.</desc>
            <constraint>
              <sch:rule xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" context="tei:note[not(@targetEnd)]">
                <sch:assert role="warning" test="@type">[S-NT] A note without targetEnd needs a
                  type.</sch:assert>
              </sch:rule>
            </constraint>
          </constraintSpec>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="annotation"><desc>an editorial annotation</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="bibl"><desc>a marginal Bible reference printed in the source</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="speaker"><desc>a speaker designation in dialogue verse</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="marginalia"><desc>a marginal note printed in the source</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="remarkResponsibility"><desc>a note on editorial responsibility</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
            <attDef ident="place" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="left"/><valItem ident="right"/><valItem ident="bottom"/>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <model cssClass="note-bibl" predicate="@type='bibl'" behaviour="inline" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.8em; color: rgb(var(--c-muted));</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="note-speaker" predicate="@type='speaker'" behaviour="inline" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.72em; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgb(var(--c-muted));</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="note-marginalia" predicate="@type='marginalia'" behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>max-width: 15em; margin: 0.3em 0 0.5em; padding-left: 0.6em; border-left: 2px solid rgb(var(--c-line)); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 1.35; color: rgb(var(--c-muted));</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model predicate="@type='remarkResponsibility'" behaviour="omit"/>
          <!-- a range comment: a numbered marker in the text, the note in the apparatus; the range
               runs from the anchor @targetEnd names to the marker -->
          <model cssClass="note-anchored" predicate="@targetEnd" behaviour="note" useSourceRendition="true">
            <param name="place" value="'end'"/>
            <param name="range" value="@targetEnd"/>
            <outputRendition>font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.62em; font-weight: 600; vertical-align: super; line-height: 0; padding: 0 0.12em; color: rgb(var(--c-accent)); text-decoration: none; scroll-margin-top: 6rem;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <!-- a comment on the whole division: no marker, shown above the text -->
          <model behaviour="note" useSourceRendition="true">
            <param name="place" value="'overview'"/>
          </model>
          <model output="plain" predicate="@targetEnd" behaviour="omit"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="list" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>A list.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="head"/><elementRef key="item"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
              <elementRef key="pb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="list">
            <outputRendition>list-style: none; margin: 0.9em 0; padding-left: 0;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="item" module="core" mode="change">
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="listItem"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="figure" module="figures" mode="change">
          <desc>A figure (woodcut, frontispiece engraving, decorative element) or notated music,
            optionally with a heading and descriptive paragraph.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <elementRef key="head"/><elementRef key="p"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
              <elementRef key="pb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="notatedMusic"><desc>notated music; <att>corresp</att> points to its
                  encoding (MEI)</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <!-- notated music is a placeholder until the MEI encoding exists -->
          <modelGrp>
            <outputRendition>margin: 1.35rem 0; padding: 1.1rem 1rem; border: 1px dashed rgb(var(--c-line)); border-radius: var(--r); text-align: center; font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgb(var(--c-muted));</outputRendition>
            <model predicate="@type='notatedMusic' and @corresp" behaviour="block">
              <param name="content" value="concat('Notensatz: ', @corresp)"/>
            </model>
            <model predicate="@type='notatedMusic'" behaviour="block">
              <param name="content" value="'Notensatz'"/>
            </model>
          </modelGrp>
          <model cssClass="figure-plain" behaviour="block">
            <outputRendition>margin: 1.2em 0; text-align: center;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <model output="plain" predicate="@type='notatedMusic'" behaviour="omit"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="cit" module="core" mode="change">
          <model behaviour="cit"/>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="quote" module="core" mode="change">
          <model behaviour="block"/>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="epigraph" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <model behaviour="block"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             CLOSERS (subscriptions, datelines, signatures)
             =================================================================== -->
        <elementSpec ident="closer" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <desc>The closing matter of a division (e.g. a dedication): salutation, dateline and
            signature.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="salute"/><elementRef key="dateline"/>
              <elementRef key="signed"/><elementRef key="rs"/><elementRef key="hi"/>
              <elementRef key="lb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <model behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>margin-top: 1.6em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="salute" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="paragraph" useSourceRendition="true"/>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="dateline" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="paragraph" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>margin: 0.3em 0;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>
        <elementSpec ident="signed" module="textstructure" mode="change">
          <content><macroRef key="macro.simlerInline"/></content>
          <model behaviour="paragraph" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>margin: 0.3em 0;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             MILESTONE / BREAK / FORME-WORK ELEMENTS
             =================================================================== -->
        <elementSpec ident="milestone" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>An empty milestone marking a structural section boundary in the source.
            <att>unit</att> is required; the rule it prints is its <att>rendition</att>
            (<val>#hr</val>, as in the DTA base format).</desc>
          <content><empty/></content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="unit" mode="change" usage="req">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="section"><desc>a section boundary within the text</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <model behaviour="block" useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>margin: 1.6em auto;</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <milestone unit="section" rendition="#hr"/>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="cb" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>Marks the beginning or end of a column. <att>type</att>=<val>start</val>/<val>end</val>
            brackets a two-column passage.</desc>
          <content><empty/></content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="start"/><valItem ident="end"/>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <model behaviour="break">
            <param name="type" value="'column'"/>
            <param name="label" value="''"/>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="anchor" module="linking" mode="change">
          <desc>An anchor point delimiting a commented range (paired with a <gi>note</gi> via
            <att>targetEnd</att>). The range is keyed either by <att>xml:id</att> or by <att>n</att>
            on a start/end pair.</desc>
          <content><empty/></content>
          <constraintSpec ident="anchor-note" scheme="schematron">
            <desc>An anchor with an <att>xml:id</att> starts the range of a following note.</desc>
            <constraint>
              <sch:rule xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" context="tei:anchor[@xml:id]">
                <sch:let name="id" value="@xml:id"/>
                <sch:assert role="warning" test="following::tei:note[replace(@targetEnd, '^#', '') = $id]">[S-AN]
                  No note comments the range this anchor starts.</sch:assert>
              </sch:rule>
            </constraint>
          </constraintSpec>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="commentRangeStart"/><valItem ident="commentRangeEnd"/>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <model behaviour="anchor"/>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="space" module="transcr" mode="change">
          <desc>A significant blank space in the source.</desc>
          <content><empty/></content>
          <model behaviour="inline">
            <outputRendition>display: inline-block; min-width: 1.5em;</outputRendition>
          </model>
        </elementSpec>

        <elementSpec ident="fw" module="transcr" mode="change">
          <desc>Forme work — running material outside the text block (page numbers, signatures,
            catchwords, running headers). <att>type</att> classifies it, <att>place</att> locates
            it.</desc>
          <content>
            <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
              <textNode/><elementRef key="hi"/><elementRef key="num"/><elementRef key="choice"/>
              <elementRef key="unclear"/><elementRef key="supplied"/><elementRef key="note"/>
              <elementRef key="head"/><elementRef key="anchor"/><elementRef key="lb"/>
            </alternate>
          </content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="pageNum"><desc>a printed page number</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="catch"><desc>a catchword</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="sig"><desc>a printer's signature</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="header"><desc>a running header</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
            <attDef ident="place" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="semi" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="top"/><valItem ident="bottom"/>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <!-- set where the print sets it, and kept out of the search index -->
          <modelGrp useSourceRendition="true">
            <outputRendition>font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.7em; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: rgb(var(--c-muted)); margin: 0.4em 0;</outputRendition>
            <model cssClass="fw-header" predicate="@type='header'" behaviour="block">
              <outputRendition>text-align: center;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model cssClass="fw-right" predicate="@type='catch' or @type='pageNum'" behaviour="block">
              <outputRendition>text-align: right;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model behaviour="block"/>
          </modelGrp>
          <model output="plain" behaviour="omit"/>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <fw type="pageNum" place="top">194</fw>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===== pb: page beginning ===== -->
        <elementSpec ident="pb" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>Marks the beginning of a new printed page. <att>n</att> gives the printed page number
            (bracketed when editorially supplied); <att>facs</att> names the page image.</desc>
          <content><empty/></content>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="n" mode="change" usage="opt"/>
            <attDef ident="facs" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <desc>The image identifier of the page, relative to the root of the IIIF manifest named by
                <gi>idno</gi> <att>type</att>=<val>URLIIIF</val> (e.g. <val>4017111</val>). Optional:
                absent for pages identified only by a printer's signature.</desc>
              <datatype><dataRef key="teidata.pointer"/></datatype>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <!-- a ruled marker across the column, `—— [16] ——`; inside a paragraph, a verse line or a
               heading it stays in the line. `data-page` opens the page in the facsimile. -->
          <modelGrp>
            <outputRendition>display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.7em; margin: 1.4em 0; font-family: var(--f-ui); font-size: 0.68em; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: rgb(var(--c-muted)); user-select: none; scroll-margin-top: 5rem;</outputRendition>
            <model cssClass="pb-inline" predicate="ancestor::p or ancestor::l or ancestor::head" behaviour="break">
              <param name="type" value="'page'"/>
              <param name="data-page" value="@facs"/>
              <param name="label" value="concat('[', translate((@n, '·')[1], '[]', ''), ']')"/>
              <outputRendition>display: inline; margin: 0 0.3em;</outputRendition>
            </model>
            <model cssClass="pb-rule" behaviour="break">
              <param name="type" value="'page'"/>
              <param name="data-page" value="@facs"/>
              <param name="label" value="concat('[', translate((@n, '·')[1], '[]', ''), ']')"/>
              <outputRendition scope="before">content: ''; flex: 1; border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--c-line));</outputRendition>
              <outputRendition scope="after">content: ''; flex: 1; border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--c-line));</outputRendition>
            </model>
          </modelGrp>
          <model output="plain" behaviour="omit"/>
          <exemplum>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <pb n="194" facs="4049203"/>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

        <!-- ===== lb: line break (DTABf semantics) ===== -->
        <elementSpec ident="lb" module="core" mode="change">
          <desc>Marks the <emph>end</emph> of a printed line (Zeilenschluss), following the DTA base
            format convention (<ref target="https://www.deutschestextarchiv.de/doku/basisformat/lbAllg.html"
            >lbAllg</ref>). Placement rules:
            <list>
              <item><gi>lb</gi> is never implicit: every line end is marked explicitly, including the
                end of the first line of a block.</item>
              <item>when a line end coincides with the end of one or more elements, the <gi>lb</gi> is
                placed <emph>after the outermost closing tag</emph>, as a following sibling of that
                element — <emph>not</emph> as the last child inside it. In particular the line end of
                the last verse line of a poem follows the closing <gi>lg</gi> (and, where the
                <gi>lg</gi> is the last child of its <gi>div</gi>, the closing <gi>div</gi>), never
                the last <gi>l</gi>.</item>
              <item>only <gi>pb</gi>, <gi>cb</gi> and <gi>space</gi> stand without a following
                <gi>lb</gi>; and no <gi>lb</gi> is set immediately before
                <gi>front</gi>/<gi>body</gi>/<gi>back</gi>/<gi>titlePage</gi> closes.</item>
              <item>for a word hyphenated across the line, the visible hyphen is kept in the
                transcription and <att>break</att>=<val>no</val> is set on the <gi>lb</gi> at that
                line end. Whitespace on either side of such an <gi>lb</gi> is not significant: the
                word is joined whatever the indentation. A hyphen that ends a word (an ellipsis,
                as in <mentioned>buß- und gnadbegierig</mentioned>) takes a plain <gi>lb</gi>.</item>
            </list>
            The Schematron constraint <ident>lb-line-end-placement</ident> checks that <gi>lb</gi> is
            not left as the last child of a line-bearing element.</desc>
          <content><empty/></content>
          <constraintSpec ident="lb-line-end-placement" scheme="schematron">
            <desc>Enforces the DTABf rule that a line break marks a line END placed after the
              outermost closing element: an <gi>lb</gi> may not be left as the last (significant)
              child of a line-bearing element such as <gi>lg</gi>, <gi>l</gi> or <gi>div</gi> — it
              should be moved to follow that element's closing tag.</desc>
            <constraint>
              <sch:rule xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron"
                context="tei:lb[not(following-sibling::*) and not(following-sibling::text()[normalize-space()])]">
                <sch:report role="warning"
                  test="parent::tei:l or parent::tei:lg or parent::tei:div or parent::tei:head
                      or parent::tei:p or parent::tei:list or parent::tei:item or parent::tei:hi
                      or parent::tei:closer or parent::tei:salute or parent::tei:signed
                      or parent::tei:dateline or parent::tei:titlePart or parent::tei:figure
                      or parent::tei:fw or parent::tei:body or parent::tei:front">
                  [S-LB] A line break (lb) marks a line END and must follow the outermost closing
                  element; here it is the last child of &lt;<sch:value-of select="local-name(parent::*)"/>&gt;.
                  Move the lb to immediately after the closing &lt;/<sch:value-of select="local-name(parent::*)"/>&gt; tag.
                </sch:report>
              </sch:rule>
            </constraint>
          </constraintSpec>
          <constraintSpec ident="lb-joined" scheme="schematron">
            <desc>A joined line end continues a word of its own line, so it does not open its
              element; the line of a catchword ends with a plain <gi>lb</gi>, as in the DTA base
              format.</desc>
            <constraint>
              <sch:rule xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" context="tei:lb[@break='no']">
                <sch:report role="warning" test="not(preceding-sibling::node()[normalize-space() or self::*])">[S-LBJ]
                  A joined line end opens its element.</sch:report>
                <sch:report role="warning" test="preceding-sibling::*[1][self::tei:fw[@type='catch']]">[S-LBC]
                  The line of a catchword ends with a plain lb.</sch:report>
              </sch:rule>
            </constraint>
          </constraintSpec>
          <attList>
            <attDef ident="break" mode="change" usage="opt">
              <valList type="closed" mode="replace">
                <valItem ident="no"><desc>the line break falls inside a word (hyphenation): the
                  following line continues the broken word</desc></valItem>
                <valItem ident="yes"><desc>the line break coincides with a word boundary (the
                  default)</desc></valItem>
              </valList>
            </attDef>
          </attList>
          <!-- A line break is dropped where the output already starts a line (after a block). At a
               hyphenated line end the print shows the hyphen — the source's own, where the
               transcription kept it, or a supplied one, in grey — and the break. The reading text
               joins every line but the title page's, and keeps the space between the words; the
               search text joins the hyphenated word and needs no space. -->
          <model cssClass="lb-hyphen" predicate="@break='no' and matches(preceding-sibling::node()[normalize-space()][1], '[-¬⸗&#xAD;&#x2010;&#x2011;]\s*$')" behaviour="break">
            <param name="type" value="'line'"/>
            <param name="label" value="'-'"/>
          </model>
          <model cssClass="lb-hyphen-supplied" predicate="@break='no'" behaviour="break">
            <param name="type" value="'line'"/>
            <param name="label" value="'-'"/>
            <outputRendition>color: rgb(var(--c-muted));</outputRendition>
          </model>
          <modelSequence>
            <model behaviour="break">
              <param name="type" value="'line'"/>
            </model>
            <model behaviour="text">
              <param name="content" value="' '"/>
            </model>
          </modelSequence>
          <model output="normalized" predicate="@break='no' or not(ancestor::titlePage)" behaviour="omit"/>
          <model output="plain" predicate="@break='no'" behaviour="omit"/>
          <model output="plain" behaviour="break">
            <param name="type" value="'line'"/>
          </model>
          <exemplum>
            <p>The line end of the last verse line follows the <emph>outermost</emph> closing element
              — here after <gi>div</gi>, as a sibling of it — not inside <gi>lg</gi> after the last
              <gi>l</gi>:</p>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <div type="poem">
                <lg type="poem">
                  <l>Die gwaltigen umsonst sich wider Christum lehnen:</l>
                  <lb/>
                  <l rendition="#et">dann Gottes rahtschluß muß fortgehen immerzu/</l>
                </lg>
              </div>
              <lb/>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
          <exemplum>
            <p>Counter-example — <emph>incorrect</emph>: the final <gi>lb</gi> must not be the last
              child of <gi>lg</gi>:</p>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <lg type="poem">
                <l>dann Gottes rahtschluß muß fortgehen immerzu/</l>
                <lb/>
              </lg>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
          <exemplum>
            <p>Hyphenation: the hyphen is retained and <att>break</att>=<val>no</val> marks the
              continuation:</p>
            <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
              <l>und Gottes wort be<lb break="no"/>trachtet/</l>
            </egXML>
          </exemplum>
        </elementSpec>

      </schemaSpec>
    </body>
  </text>
</TEI>
